      <role>Decode the instruction, read the register file, extend immediates, resolve forwarding for decode-time compare, and capture IF/ID state.</role>
      <operations>
        <op order="1">U_RF reads RR1=ID_rs1 and RR2=ID_rs2 and later writes WB_WD to WR when WB_RFWrite is high.</op>
        <op order="2">U_EXT sign-extends or zero-extends Imm12. In the current decoder, signed extension is used for all implemented immediate paths.</op>
        <op order="3">ControlUnit computes the main control outputs RFWrite, DMCtrl, PCWrite, IRWrite, InsMemRW, ExtSel, ALUOp, NPCOp, ALUSrcA, ALUSrcB, RegSel, and WDSel from opcode and funct fields.</op>
        <op order="4">ControlUnit performs decode-stage forwarding so that ID_RD1_out and ID_RD2_out may come from EX, MEM, or WB instead of raw RF outputs.</op>
        <op order="5">ID_zero is generated by direct compare of ID_RD1_out and ID_RD2_out and later drives branch intent generation.</op>
        <op order="6">ControlUnit latches decoded control and data into the IF/ID register group.</op>
      </operations>
