  <implementationNotes>
    <note severity="important" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/riscv.v:128-131">RegSel is generated by ControlUnit but the actual top-level destination mux control is hard-wired to RegSel_rd, so WR always equals WB_rd.</note>
    <note severity="important" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/ControlUnit.v:148-154">EX-stage forwarding placeholders EX_RD1_out and EX_RD2_out exist, but the top-level does not use them and the forwarding logic is commented out.</note>
    <note severity="important" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/IR.v:3-10">IR is not a clocked register; it is a combinational gate that outputs zero when IRWrite is low.</note>
    <note severity="important" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/riscv.v:179-184">The optional load-data register U_DR is commented out. DR_out is directly assigned from RD.</note>
    <note severity="important" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/riscv.v:166,cpu/rtl/rtl/ControlUnit.v:143-146">ALU.zero is generated, but the active branch compare path uses cu_zero from ControlUnit.ID_zero rather than the ALU zero output.</note>
    <note severity="important" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/MUX_2to1_A.v:3-10,cpu/rtl/rtl/ControlUnit.v:156-295">ALUSrcA exists, but the alternate input on U_MUX_2to1_A is hard-wired to 5'h0 and the current decode does not actively select it for implemented instructions.</note>
    <note severity="info" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/ControlUnit.v:103-105">State, NxtState, and the AR/MEM/WB/EX bookkeeping registers are declared, but the current controller behavior is direct combinational decode plus distributed pipeline flops rather than an active finite state machine.</note>
    <note severity="info" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/PC.v:32-47">PCWrite is initialized high and never deasserted by the current decoder. Stalls are modeled through PC_NPC and IM_PC path selection rather than by freezing the PC register with PCWrite low.</note>
    <note severity="info" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/IM.v:13-19,cpu/rtl/rtl/DM.v:15-22">Both instruction and data memories are modeled as word arrays with synchronous always blocks.</note>
    <note severity="info" source="cpu/rtl/rtl/riscv.v:186-191,cpu/rtl/rtl/RF.v:37-43">DPI exports are enabled by the difftest macro so the testbench can observe committed PC and architectural registers.</note>
  </implementationNotes>
